From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] plat: ecnt: bl2: room for a larger BL33 on parallel NAND

BL2 loads the LZMA-compressed BL33 into EN7523_IMAGE_BUF (0x58000) and
unpacks it below BL33_LIMIT (1 MiB).  The compressed image and the LZMA
decoder's ~16 KiB of probabilities share that buffer, so U-Boot has to
stay under about 344 KiB packed and 1 MiB unpacked.  With the raw NAND
stack the FiberHome HG5382A U-Boot is over both, and BL2 stops with

  ERROR:   BL2: Failed to load image id 5 (-27)

(-EFBIG from load_image(), whose size check the pre-image-load hook
points at the decompression buffer).

For the parallel NAND BL2 only, widen the buffer to 0x80000 and let BL33
unpack up to 2 MiB.  The buffer still ends at 0x81900000, far below
BL33_BASE; up to 0x82000000 nothing else is in use while BL2 runs.
SPI-NAND builds are unchanged, so their limits still match the BL2s
already out in the field.
---
 plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h b/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h
--- a/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h
+++ b/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h
@@ -177,7 +177,16 @@
 #define TZRAM2_LIMIT		(TZRAM2_BASE + TZRAM2_SIZE)
 
 #define	BL33_BASE			(EN7523_MEM_BASE + UL(0x1E00000))
+#if defined(TCSUPPORT_PARALLEL_NAND)
+/*
+ * U-Boot with the raw NAND stack unpacks to more than 1 MiB.  Nothing else
+ * lives up to 0x82000000 while BL2 runs; U-Boot's own early stack sits there
+ * afterwards anyway.
+ */
+#define BL33_LIMIT			(BL33_BASE + UL(0x200000))
+#else
 #define BL33_LIMIT			(BL33_BASE + UL(0x100000))
+#endif
 
 #ifdef TCSUPPORT_OPTEE
 //#define BL32_BASE           (BL31_LIMIT + UL(0x1000))
@@ -216,9 +225,18 @@
 #else
 #define EN7523_IMAGE_BUF_OFFSET		(PLAT_ECNT_FIP_BASE + UL(0x80000))
 #endif
+#if defined(TCSUPPORT_PARALLEL_NAND)
+/*
+ * Holds the LZMA BL33 as read from the FIP plus the decoder's ~16 KiB of
+ * state; 0x58000 leaves no room for the parallel NAND U-Boot.  The buffer
+ * still ends far below BL33_BASE.
+ */
+#define EN7523_IMAGE_BUF_SIZE		UL(0x80000)
+#else
 #define EN7523_IMAGE_BUF_SIZE		UL(0x58000)
 #endif
 #endif
+#endif
 
 #ifdef TCSUPPORT_BL2_OPTIMIZATION
 #ifdef IMAGE_BL21
-- 
